Patch 03 (repro-cops): primal-chain track and its reviewer use absolute main-tree paths.

Problem: publication/primal/chain/{build_points,verify_points,scip_crosscheck}.py and
publication/reviews/primal-chain-r1/rev_chain_exact.py set HERE/TRACK/PRIMAL/BOUND/OSIL to
literal /workspace/local-home/... paths, so in a clean checkout they read and WRITE the main tree.
Fix: paths relative to the script location (HERE = dirname(__file__), R29 = three levels up)
and the expanduser OSIL path. Outputs are unchanged except that the metadata field
"source_point" of points/chainN_generator.json records the checkout's absolute path (it is
written, never read). rev_negative_controls.py imports rev_chain_exact, so its printed assert
line numbers shift by 2.  Apply:  git apply 03-primal-chain-scripts-relative-paths.patch

